<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH C.BANK SEES ROOM FOR POSSIBLE RATE CUT.</title>
<headline>CZECH C.BANK SEES ROOM FOR POSSIBLE RATE CUT.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech National Bank Governor Josef Tosovsky said on Thursday the favourable development in the key money supply measure, M2, in 1996 has created a good basis for possibly reducing inflation and interest rates.</p>
<p>&quot;The reduction of M2 in 1996 created a good basis for the future reduction of inflation and possibly of interest rates,&quot; he told a news conference.</p>
</text>
